---
// MultiDisciplineBmsMindMap.astro
// Interactive / Graphical Mind Map linking all fields needed to resolve BMS
---

<div class="bms-mindmap-container">
	<div class="mindmap-header">
		<span class="mindmap-kicker">Interactive System Matrix</span>
		<h3 class="mindmap-main-title">The Cross-Discipline BMS Resolution&nbsp;Map</h3>
		<p class="mindmap-subtitle">
			Burning Mouth Syndrome cannot be diagnosed or resolved within a single medical silo. Click or hover on any discipline to see why that field holds a critical piece of the&nbsp;puzzle.
		</p>
	</div>

	<!-- Central Hub & Orbital Nodes -->
	<div class="mindmap-canvas">
		<!-- Central Core Node -->
		<div class="mindmap-core">
			<div class="core-circle">
				<span class="core-icon">🎯</span>
				<span class="core-title">BMS RESOLUTION</span>
				<span class="core-sub">Systemic Unification</span>
			</div>
			<!-- Pulsing Ambient Ring -->
			<div class="core-glow-ring"></div>
		</div>

		<!-- Surrounding Discipline Cards -->
		<div class="mindmap-nodes-grid">
			<!-- Node 1: Restorative Dentistry -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-dentistry">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🦷</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Restorative Dentistry</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Physical Hardware</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Controls crowns, fillings, margins, and cervical NCCLs. Aging cements and micro-gaps allow acidic fluids to leak directly into porous dentin.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Eliminates physical micro-leaks and unsealed tubules that fuel the burning.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 2: Oral Medicine & Perio -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-perio">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🩺</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Periodontology &amp; Oral Med</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Mucosal Barrier</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Manages gingival recession, root cementum exposure, and subgingival biofilm. Bridges hard enamel surfaces with fragile mucosal tissue.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Recession exposes unshielded root tubules to friction and chemical irritation.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 3: Clinical Neurology -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-neurology">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🧠</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Clinical Neurology</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Central Sensitization</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Decodes trigeminal nerve pathways and brainstem "wind-up." Low-grade continuous peripheral firing lowers pain thresholds, causing diffuse oral burning.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Explains why localized tooth leaks radiate as whole-mouth tongue and palate burning.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 4: Molecular Neuroscience -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-neuroscience">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">⚡</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Molecular Neuroscience</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Ion Channel Receptors</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Pinpoints Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (ASIC1, ASIC3), TRPV1, and TRPM8. Proves protons (H⁺) physically depolarize unmyelinated C-fibers.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Removes the "psychosomatic" label by identifying concrete molecular switches.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 5: Gastroenterology & Medicine -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-gastro">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🔬</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Medicine &amp; Gastroenterology</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Reflux &amp; Saliva Buffering</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Catches silent nocturnal acid reflux (LPR/GERD), Sjögren's, and salivary gland dysfunction that depletes bicarbonate and strips tooth pellicles.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Identifies hidden endogenous acid floods that dissolve protective tubule plugs overnight.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 6: Biochemistry & Nutrition -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-biochem">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🥩</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Biochemistry &amp; Nutrition</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Chemical Fuel Input</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Tracks dietary acids (citric, acetic, phosphoric) and fermentable sugars that oral bacteria ferment into lactic acid against teeth.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Elimination protocols (low-acid or carnivore) shut down the chemical fuel supply immediately.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 7: Legal & Patient Rights -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-legal">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">⚖️</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Legal &amp; Patient Data Rights</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Records Ownership</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Enforces patient legal rights (HIPAA, PIPEDA, Law 25) to full digital records, raw DICOM X-rays, perio charts, and unedited clinical notes.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Empowers patients to conduct forensic time-series audits without clinic gatekeeping.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 8: Professional Orders -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-orders">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">🏛️</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Professional Orders &amp; Boards</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Scopes of Practice</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Governs the regulatory boundaries between dental and medical colleges. The current divide traps BMS in a jurisdictional void where neither takes ownership.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Must establish updated interdisciplinary guidelines so doctors and dentists can co-manage patients safely.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Node 9: Systems Engineering -->
			<div class="discipline-card card-engineering">
				<div class="card-header-bar">
					<span class="card-icon">⚙️</span>
					<div class="card-header-text">
						<h4 class="card-title">Systems Engineering</h4>
						<span class="card-tag">Root-Cause Architecture</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="card-summary">
					Applies failure-mode analysis (FMEA), baseline logging, and systematic variable elimination to connect fragmented medical clues into a coherent circuit.
				</p>
				<div class="card-key-factor">
					<strong>Critical Link:</strong> Treats the patient as the Chief Systems Orchestrator who synthesizes all disparate clues.
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Bottom Takeaway Bar -->
	<div class="mindmap-footer-takeaway">
		<div class="takeaway-badge">Core Principle</div>
		<p class="takeaway-text">
			When each specialty works in isolation, BMS is declared an incurable mystery. When all nine disciplines are connected as a unified circuit, the root causes become clear, measurable, and systematically&nbsp;treatable.
		</p>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.bms-mindmap-container {
		background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0d081a 0%, #150f26 100%);
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35);
		border-radius: 24px;
		padding: 2.75rem 2rem;
		margin: 3rem auto;
		color: #ffffff;
		box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
		max-width: 1040px;
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	.mindmap-header {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
		padding: 0 1rem;
	}

	.mindmap-kicker {
		display: inline-block;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: #c084fc;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.mindmap-main-title {
		font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
		font-weight: 800;
		color: #ffffff;
		line-height: 1.15;
		margin: 0 auto 0.75rem auto;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.mindmap-subtitle {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: rgba(233, 213, 255, 0.85);
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	/* Canvas & Grid */
	.mindmap-canvas {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 2.5rem;
		position: relative;
	}

	/* Central Core */
	.mindmap-core {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: center;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.core-circle {
		width: 200px;
		height: 200px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%, #7e22ce 0%, #3b0764 100%);
		border: 3px solid #c084fc;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		text-align: center;
		padding: 1rem;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		box-shadow: 0 0 35px rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4), inset 0 2px 4px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
		z-index: 2;
	}

	.core-icon {
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		line-height: 1;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}

	.core-title {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		font-weight: 900;
		color: #ffffff;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		line-height: 1.15;
	}

	.core-sub {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: #e9d5ff;
		margin-top: 0.25rem;
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.core-glow-ring {
		position: absolute;
		width: 230px;
		height: 230px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		border: 1px dashed rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.4);
		animation: rotateRing 30s linear infinite;
	}

	@keyframes rotateRing {
		from { transform: rotate(0deg); }
		to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
	}

	/* Discipline Nodes Grid */
	.mindmap-nodes-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1.25rem;
		width: 100%;
	}

	.discipline-card {
		background: rgba(26, 17, 43, 0.85);
		border-radius: 18px;
		padding: 1.35rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		justify-content: space-between;
		border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
		transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.discipline-card:hover {
		transform: translateY(-4px);
		box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
	}

	/* Discipline Card Specific Accent Colors */
	.card-dentistry {
		border-top: 4px solid #10b981;
	}
	.card-dentistry:hover { border-color: #10b981; }

	.card-perio {
		border-top: 4px solid #14b8a6;
	}
	.card-perio:hover { border-color: #14b8a6; }

	.card-neurology {
		border-top: 4px solid #3b82f6;
	}
	.card-neurology:hover { border-color: #3b82f6; }

	.card-neuroscience {
		border-top: 4px solid #8b5cf6;
	}
	.card-neuroscience:hover { border-color: #8b5cf6; }

	.card-gastro {
		border-top: 4px solid #f59e0b;
	}
	.card-gastro:hover { border-color: #f59e0b; }

	.card-biochem {
		border-top: 4px solid #ef4444;
	}
	.card-biochem:hover { border-color: #ef4444; }

	.card-legal {
		border-top: 4px solid #06b6d4;
	}
	.card-legal:hover { border-color: #06b6d4; }

	.card-orders {
		border-top: 4px solid #ec4899;
	}
	.card-orders:hover { border-color: #ec4899; }

	.card-engineering {
		border-top: 4px solid #a855f7;
	}
	.card-engineering:hover { border-color: #a855f7; }

	.card-header-bar {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
	}

	.card-icon {
		font-size: 1.85rem;
		line-height: 1;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}

	.card-header-text {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.card-title {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}

	.card-tag {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgba(216, 180, 254, 0.85);
		margin-top: 0.15rem;
	}

	.card-summary {
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: #cbd5e1;
		margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.card-key-factor {
		background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
		border-radius: 10px;
		padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: #e2e8f0;
		border-left: 3px solid rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.6);
	}

	.card-key-factor strong {
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	/* Footer Takeaway */
	.mindmap-footer-takeaway {
		margin-top: 2.75rem;
		background: rgba(88, 28, 135, 0.25);
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35);
		border-radius: 16px;
		padding: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.takeaway-badge {
		background: #7e22ce;
		color: #ffffff;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
		border-radius: 8px;
		white-space: nowrap;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}

	.takeaway-text {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: #f1f5f9;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	@media (max-width: 980px) {
		.mindmap-nodes-grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 680px) {
		.bms-mindmap-container {
			padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
		}

		.mindmap-nodes-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.mindmap-footer-takeaway {
			flex-direction: column;
			align-items: flex-start;
			gap: 0.75rem;
		}
	}
</style>
